  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Can GIRAFFE be run with my own optimizer settings? For our 52 rice leaf samples from the drought trial I want a learning rate of 1e-4, 2,000 iterations and a heavier weight on the PPI term in the loss, because in a pilot the package defaults gave a TF activity matrix that looked over-smoothed and I'd like to see whether these settings change that."
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "What I understood you are asking for:\n1. \"a TF activity matrix\" -- not available here: no registered workflow produces this. PANDA does not give it: the PPI network is an input of possible TF cooperation. PANDA refines a cooperativity matrix internally, but the executor does not save it, and it is not a measurement of physical complexes or stoichiometry.\n2. \"a learning rate of 1e-4\" -- not available here as asked. NetZoo runs GIRAFFE with its package defaults and passes no settings to it, so \"a learning rate of 1e-4\" cannot be applied.\n3. \"2,000 iterations\" -- not available here as asked. NetZoo runs GIRAFFE with its package defaults and passes no settings to it, so \"2,000 iterations\" cannot be applied.\n4. \"a heavier weight on the PPI term in the loss\" -- not available here as asked. NetZoo runs GIRAFFE with its package defaults and passes no settings to it, so \"a heavier weight on the PPI term in the loss\" cannot be applied.\n\nNo registered workflow can give these as you asked them (above), so none is offered as asked.\n\nNo files were inspected and no analysis ran."
    }
  ],
